invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: take_share holds a key_exchange to at least its group's length
  rather than exactly that many, so a 33-byte x25519 share or a
  1217-byte X25519MLKEM768 share is handed to the key exchange, which
  reads the length it expects and agrees on a key the client computed
  from different bytes. srv_parser.h fixes each length, and
  test/srv_parser_tests.h requires illegal_parameter one byte over it as
  well as one byte under, for both groups.

--- old
    if (share_len != (hybrid ? CH_HYBRID_CLIENT_SHARE : X25519_LEN)) {
--- new
    if (share_len < (hybrid ? CH_HYBRID_CLIENT_SHARE : X25519_LEN)) {
